 "rules": [
  {
   "evidence": "day10 trace cycles 264-274 + day-10 record close .dat parse",
   "id": "R1",
   "rule": "COUNT FROM STATE, NEVER FROM DIGS. Progress on every material (logs, planks, sticks, cobble) is counted only from the inventory read-back in the driver's state. A dig result of ok increments nothing. Day-10 proof: cycle 274 declared 'Eight cobble!' from 8 dig-ok results; the close .dat held cobblestone x1."
  },
  {
   "evidence": "day10 trace cycles 264-274 (pos + dig rows). NEGATIVE ARM PROVEN (two episodes); POSITIVE ARM UNPROVEN - no held trace shows seam-stance pickup; nearest positive evidence is felltree's 'gathered drops' when the body moves through drop cells.",
   "id": "R2",
   "rule": "STAND IN THE SEAM. Before digging a stone seam laterally, move the body INTO the seam row (feet at the seam floor's level, inside the cavity row) so drops spawn at the body's feet. Never dig a seam row from a stance above it. Day-10 episode 1: body fixed at (89.7,67,-105.5) for cycles 264-273, seam at y64 three below; 8 drops left in the row, 0 collected."
  },
  {
   "evidence": "day10 trace cycles 296-302",
   "id": "R3",
   "rule": "NEVER CHASE A DESCENDING SEAM DOWNWARD. Work a seam at ONE level. Digging a block 2+ below the body's feet from a fixed stance opens a hollow under the drops. If the seam descends, first step down onto the seam floor by digging the foot-level block in front, or abandon the seam for a level one. Day-10 episode 2: cycles 298-300 dug y62, y61, y60 from stances at y65/y63; 4+ drops fell into the hollow past reach."
  },
  {
   "evidence": "day10 trace cycles 63, 301",
   "id": "R4",
   "rule": "COLLECT IS NOT A RECOVERY VERB. On day 10 collect was issued twice (cycles 63 and 301) and reported 'visited 0' both times; at cycle 301 it saw 3 drops and gathered none provably (inventory stayed 1). Recovery of a drop = move the body's feet onto the drop's cell (goto the cell), never collect from a stance."
  },
  {
   "evidence": "day3 trace (furnace crafts), day9 trace cycles 7/9/11, day10 trace cycles 201, 281-287. The F2 recovery (planks recraft -> dependent crafts succeed) was observed once (day10 285->287) and contradicted once (day10 282->283): filed as heuristic, not proven rule.",
   "id": "R5",
   "rule": "CRAFT DISCIPLINE. (F1) If a craft failure NAMES an ingredient ('missing ingredients - X - you hold A of B'), craft or fetch X and retry ONCE. (F2) If it names an ingredient the citizen has NEVER held (the cherry_planks phantom, days 9-10: the resolver keys some recipes to cherry_planks he does not hold), re-craft planks once, then retry once; a second phantom failure STOPS the chain and is filed - do not loop. (F3) If the failure names NOTHING ('no craftable recipe for furnace at table', day 3 x8), read the inventory and name the shortage from state yourself; if state shows no shortage, suspect table reach: goto the table cell and retry once. NEVER repeat an identical failed craft more than once without an intervening state change (day 3 repeated the identical failing furnace craft at cycles 8, 68, 80, 82, 96, 145, 146, 234)."
  },
  {
   "evidence": "day10 record action-curve table + trace cycles 275-280",
   "id": "R6",
   "rule": "MOVEMENT TAX IS PRICED, AND CLIMB DOES NOT EXIST. Day-10 rates: goto arrival 49/136 (36%), climb 0/13, dig 58/83, craft 15/22, place 3/6. Price every goto leg at 3 attempts and use SHORT HOPS (2-4 blocks) on broken relief - Cody's own discovered technique, 4 of 6 arrivals on the day-10 home leg (cycles 275-280) vs 36% overall. This plan contains NO climb step: level changes are by dig (down) and place (up) only."
  }
 ],
